      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. That holds for every indication, including depression, OCD, PTSD, and panic disorder. Doses above 200 mg carry a higher risk of serotonin syndrome, QT effects, GI bleeding, hyponatremia, and seizures. This patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nPlease check these before we go further:\n- **Possible typo or unit error:** Did you mean 100 mg or 200 mg? 40 mg and 400 mg are also easy to mix up.\n- **Intended dose:** Typical starting doses are 25\u201350 mg daily. Titration is usually in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least a week, up to a maximum of 200 mg/day.\n- **Deliberate supratherapeutic dosing:** If your attending or psychiatry consult wants this, it needs their explicit sign-off. Please bring it to them or to pharmacy first.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, for example 50 mg or 200 mg by mouth once daily, I'll enter it right away. If the 400 mg is intentional, tell me who approved it and I can add that to the order note. I'd still recommend pharmacy review first."
      }
     ],
